========================================================================================================================
                                     ATTACHING THE NEW BRIDGE TO A SPECIFIC VM
========================================================================================================================

METHOD 1: LIVE & PERMANENT ATTACHMENT (RECOMMENDED)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Use this command to attach the network interface to a running VM immediately and ensure it persists after a reboot.

Command  | virsh attach-interface --domain my-vm --type network --source default --model virtio --live --config
         |
Fields   | --domain  : The name of your virtual machine (e.g., my-vm).
         | --type    : The type of connection interface (network).
         | --source  : The name of the virsh network (e.g., default).
         | --model   : The driver model (virtio delivers the best performance).
         | --live    : Injects the interface into the running VM without a reboot.
         | --config  : Saves the change permanently to the VM's XML configuration.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
METHOD 2: EDITING THE VM CONFIGURATION MANUALLY
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If you prefer managing configurations manually, update the VM's XML file directly.

Step 1   | Open the VM configuration:
         | virsh edit my-vm
         |
Step 2   | Find the <devices> section and paste the following block inside it:
         | 
         | <interface type='network'>
         |   <source network='default'/>
         |   <model type='virtio'/>
         | </interface>
         |
Step 3   | Save and close the editor. If the VM is running, restart it to apply:
         | virsh reboot my-vm

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Command  | Check the VM's active interfaces:
         | virsh domiflist my-vm
